---
title: Cranberry Apple Coffee Cake
description: A soft, fluffy vegan coffee cake full of apples and cranberries and topped with a thick layer of sweet crumbs. Easy to make in one #9 x 13-inch pan{}9 x 13 pan, and even better with a second cup of coffee.
image: https://www.theppk.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Apple-Cake_WEB-16.jpg
course: Breakfast, Dessert
prep time: 20 minutes
time required: 1 hour 10 minutes
tags: 
- coffee cake
- tested with gf flour
source: Modified from https://www.theppk.com/2026/09/vegan-apple-coffee-cake/
servings: 12
---

Preheat the oven to 350°F. Lightly grease a #9 x 13-inch pan{}.

Toss the @Honeycrisp apples{2%cups}(peeled and diced into 1/2-inch pieces) and the @Cranberries{2%cups}(fresh or frozen) with @granulated sugar{2%tablespoons}  and @lemon juice{1%tablespoon}. Set aside for about 10 minutes while you make the crumb topping and batter.

== Crumb topping ==

In a small mixing bowl, mix together @all-purpose flour{2%cups}, @granulated sugar{1/2%cup}, @brown sugar{1/3%cup}, and @baking powder{1/2%teaspoon}. Cut in the @refined coconut oil{1/2%cup}(at room temperature) with your fingers or a pastry cutter until you have mostly large crumbs. Some sandy bits are fine.

== Cake ==

In a large mixing bowl, whisk together the @unsweetened vegan milk{1 1/2%cups}, @olive oil{1/2%cup}, @unsweetened applesauce{1/3%cup}, @pure vanilla extract{1%tablespoon} and @apple cider vinegar{2%teaspoons}. Sift in the @all-purpose flour{2 1/2%cups}, @granulated sugar{2/3%cup}, @baking powder{4%teaspoons} and @salt{1%teaspoon} and mix just until smooth.

Fold in the fruit.

Pour the batter into the prepared pan. Sprinkle the crumb topping evenly over the top and pat it down just a little.

Bake for 45 to 50 minutes, until a knife inserted into the center comes out clean or with just a few moist crumbs attached.

Let cool for at least an hour before slicing. Dust with @powdered sugar{} and serve!

> Variations and substitutions:
>Can swap the all-purpose flour with gluten-free baking mix, I used King Arthur Measure for Measure. 
>

> Note: 
>I had to cook it for an hour.